@startuml
!include common-style.puml

title Use Case Diagram — Phase 2 (Part 1)\nAppointment, Queue, Vital Signs

top to bottom direction

actor Admin #DBEAFE
actor Receptionist #CCFBF1
actor Nurse #FEF9C3
actor Doctor #DCFCE7

rectangle "4N Clinic — Appointment, Queue & Vitals" {

  package "Appointment Scheduling" {
    usecase "UC19\nBook appointment" as UC19
    usecase "UC20\nManage appointments" as UC20
    usecase "UC21\nCheck-in to visit" as UC21
  }

  package "Queue Management" {
    usecase "UC22\nManage queue" as UC22
    usecase "UC22a\nCall patient" as UC22a
    usecase "UC22b\nTrack queue status" as UC22b
  }

  package "Vital Signs" {
    usecase "UC23\nRecord vital signs" as UC23
    usecase "UC24\nAuto-calculate BMI" as UC24
  }
}

Receptionist --> UC19
Receptionist --> UC20
Receptionist --> UC21
Receptionist --> UC22
Receptionist --> UC22a

Nurse --> UC22
Nurse --> UC22b
Nurse --> UC23
Nurse --> UC24

Doctor --> UC20

Admin --> UC20

UC21 .> UC19 : check-in from booking
UC22a .> UC22 : <<include>>
UC22b .> UC22 : <<include>>
UC24 .> UC23 : <<include>>

note bottom of UC21
UC21: convert appointment to visit.
Creates Visit record with status WAITING
and assigns queue number automatically.
end note

@enduml
